# Parallel Task Execution Reasoning - Epic 02

Epic: `02-pipeline-tts-integration`
Task count: 3

## Phase Summary

| Phase | Task | Mode | Risk | Reason |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `run-tts-after-translation-success` | main | high | Adds the initial TTS insertion point after text persistence succeeds. |
| 2 | `skip-existing-successful-tts-artifacts` | main | high | Must be inserted before the paid provider call in the exact Phase 1 control flow. |
| 3 | `record-tts-failure-without-failing-text-result` | main | high | Wraps the finalized TTS path so audio failures do not fail completed text translations. |

## Parallel-Safe Tasks

None approved in this epic.

## Why Tasks Cannot Be Parallelized

- All three tasks modify the same pipeline control flow.
- `skip-existing-successful-tts-artifacts` needs the first TTS call path before it can place the idempotency guard correctly.
- `record-tts-failure-without-failing-text-result` needs the generation, upload, and skip behavior in place before it can isolate the right failures.
- Parallel edits would conflict logically even if Git merged them, because order determines billing behavior and job success semantics.

